# Rename or copy this file to HALT (no extension) to stop the harness.
#
# The kill switch is the presence of the file named by HALT_FILE in .env, which
# defaults to HALT at the repository root. Contents are never read. The harness
# checks for it at the entry of every stage and in clone preflight; when it is
# there, `harness run` releases its clone, leaves the item resumable, and exits 5.
#
#   harness halt     creates it
#   harness resume   removes it
#
# HALT is in .gitignore. This example file is committed; the switch itself is not.
